+# Research Engine — Phase 8: The project brief, the language corpus, waves across runs (10-10-2026)
+
+**Source:** the three items proposed after the audit roadmap (Phases 1–7) closed, taken together as one phase: a *project brief* entity (the audit's §D "low" row "a project brief entity"), a *language regression corpus* built from what researchers actually type (so the recognisers and the lexicon are checked against real usage, and the sentences the engine hands on become the lexicon's backlog), and *wave trends across runs* (the one piece of §D's "findings synthesis beyond the plan" Phase 4 left open: Phase 4 reads waves inside one run; a tracker is run again). Every change has a regression test and the tests were mutation-checked. Nothing existing was removed: `set_research` keeps every field it kept, a run without a previous one has no comparison and no slide, a history without the new intent keys still makes a corpus (the record's source decides), the deck's and the report's existing sections are where they were.
+
+## Checklist
+
+| ID | Item | Change | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| B1 | A project brief entity: the client, the business question, the decision the findings inform, the background, the stakeholders, the deadline, the deliverables | `ResearchDesign.brief` (`packages/schema`, `ResearchBrief`); `set_research { brief }` **merges field by field** (coerced from the model, blanks dropped, an empty brief not carried; `describeAction` "Record the project brief (client)"); the change tree names each field (client, business question, decision, …), not "research design" | ✅ |
+| B2 | The brief by sentence | a `brief` recogniser: "the client is Acme Foods", "set the business question to …" (the sentence's own question mark comes back), "this study informs the decision to launch …" → *whether to launch …*, "the stakeholders are A, B and C", "add stakeholder: X" (never twice), "the findings are due by …", "background: …", "the deliverables are …"; *already so* when nothing would change; "what is the brief?" / "show the project brief" answers with every field (and says how to record one when there is none) | ✅ |
+| B3 | Carried into every output | the outline every model turn reads opens with `Project brief: …`; the **proposal** opens with the background, the business question, the decision and the stakeholders before the objective, carries "Findings due …" on the cover and in Sample and fieldwork, and the brief's deliverables when the design lists them; the **findings report** and the **deck** name the brief's client (the output route and the report draft prefer it to the project's client name); the deck's summary opens with the business question and the decision; the **workflow**'s objective step, with a brief and no objective, offers the business question as the objective ("Should we cut the price of Brand A?" → "Understand whether to cut the price of Brand A") | ✅ |
+| B4 | Editable by hand, reusable across projects | the research design editor's *Project brief* section (`rd-brief-*`, stakeholders and deliverables as lists); *Copy from another project…* (`GET /api/briefs`: the briefs of the caller's own projects, newest first, from each project's draft) | ✅ |
+| C1 | A language corpus from History | `packages/engine/src/languageCorpus.ts`: `corpusFromHistory(def, records)` — one entry per distinct sentence (case and spacing aside), counted, the last reading, a revised proposal's last sentence, fixes/imports/context left out; `replayCorpus` reads every sentence again with the engine as it is and says **same / better / worse / changed** (the actions compared op by op; a hand-off to the grammar's read-only answers is the grammar's, not the model's); `recordCorpus`, `describeReplay` | ✅ |
+| C2 | History records what a replay needs | every record's `intent` now carries `engine` (the engine's kind, or `model` when handed on), `engineCategory` and `engineReason` on a model record, `ops` on an actions record, `selected` (the selection the sentence was read with) | ✅ |
+| C3 | The corpus in the Studio | the History tab's *This project's language* line: sentences, how many the engine reads, the model's backlog (most said first, up to 8 shown); *Export the language corpus* (`POST /api/copilot/corpus`, `project.read`; the sandbox sends its survey) — the corpus as a file, or with `replay` the replay too | ✅ |
+| C4 | The regression gate | `packages/engine/corpus/brand-tracker.json` (the public docs' 105-sentence catalogue on the brand tracker, recorded); `languageCorpus.test.ts` replays every file in `packages/engine/corpus` and fails on anything worse or changed; `scripts/corpus-replay.mjs <file>` prints the replay (exit 1 when anything is worse) and `--record` rewrites a corpus after a deliberate change | ✅ |
+| W1 | A KPI snapshot per run | `packages/analytics/src/waves.ts` `kpiSnapshot(def, dataset)`: every KPI of the design measured as the design says — `top-2-box share` (any `top-N`), `mean` (with the sd the comparison needs), `NPS`, `share <option>`; "no variable" / "not in this run's data" when it cannot be; `run.kpis`, printed in the brief the model reads, stored (`analytics_runs.kpis`, migration 0049, inserted with a fallback without it) | ✅ |
+| W2 | The comparison with the previous run | `compareRuns(current, previous)`: each KPI's last and current value, the delta, the move's significance on the two samples (a two-proportion test for shares and box shares, Welch's t from the two summaries for a mean), better/worse by the KPI's direction (flat under 0.05); the planned findings matched by **what they test** (`findingKey`: the plan item and its variables — never the hash, which the dataset spec is part of) as new / stronger / weaker / reversed / same, and those no longer found; the verdicts that changed; a one-line summary. Attached as `run.since` by whoever has the previous run: `runPlanFor` (the latest earlier run on the same environment and dataset kind — a clean milestone run is not compared with an "all" run), the output route (the latest stored run; the sandbox may send `previous`), stored (`analytics_runs.since`) | ✅ |
+| W3 | Told everywhere the same way | the Findings tab's KPI table (last wave, this wave, the change with ● significant / ○ not, better/worse) and *Since the last wave* (the changed findings with was/now, the changed verdicts, what is no longer found); the brief the model reads (`describeSince`); the narrative gate knows the deltas (`waveNumbers`); the deck's `wave_change` slide right after the summary (the KPI table and the changes beside it); the report's *Since the last wave* section after the hypotheses; the report's `x-rescript-output` names the previous run | ✅ |
+
+## What was built
+
+**The brief (`packages/schema`, `packages/engine`)** — `ResearchBrief { client?, businessQuestion?, decision?, background?, stakeholders[], deadline?, deliverables[] }` on `research.brief`. `set_research.brief` is a partial: the apply merges `{ stakeholders: [], deliverables: [], ...prev, ...given }`, so "the client is Acme" never loses the business question. `BRIEF_WORDS` names the fields in descriptions. `objectiveFromBusinessQuestion` turns a yes/no question into an objective ("Is Brand A losing younger buyers?" → "Understand whether …", a wh-question → "Understand why …", a statement kept). The brief recogniser sits between `objective` and `audience`.
+
+**The corpus (`packages/engine/src/languageCorpus.ts`)** — `LanguageCorpus { version: 1, exported, survey, definition, entries }`; `CorpusEntry { text, kind, category?, ops?, selected?, count?, at? }`; kinds are the engine's plus `model` and `grammar`. `readingOf` is the compact reading the corpus records (kind, category, ops, understood). Verdicts: same (kind equal; for actions, ops equal), better (model's or grammar's → the engine's), worse (the engine's → the model's), changed (anything else — a sentence refused as "already so" against the survey as it is now is *changed*, honestly). The backlog is what is *now* the model's, most said first.
+
+**Waves (`packages/analytics/src/waves.ts`)** — `KpiSnapshot`, `KpiDelta`, `FindingChange`, `VerdictChange`, `WaveComparison`; `kpiSnapshot`, `compareRuns`, `findingKey`, `waveNumbers`, `describeSince`. `AnalysisRun.kpis` and `.since`; `runPlan` fills the KPIs; `briefText` prints both; `narrative.runNumbers` admits the wave numbers; `deck.ts` `waveSlide` and the `wave_change` slide type (drawn by `export/deck.ts` as a table with a legend and the changes beside); `export/docx.ts` the section. `apps/studio/lib/analyticsRunStore.ts` `pickPrevious(rows, datasetKind)`; `apps/studio/lib/analytics.ts` `previousRun(db, surveyId, spec, before)`; `runPlanFor` attaches the comparison before storing; the cron's milestone runs get it for free.
+
+**The Studio** — `ResearchDesignEditor` `BriefSection`; `CopilotPanel` `LanguageSection` (History); `FindingsTab` `fd-kpis` / `fd-kpi` (`data-verdict`, `data-significant`) / `fd-kpi-delta` / `fd-since` / `fd-since-finding` / `fd-since-verdict` / `fd-since-gone`; `useCopilot.exportCorpus`; routes `POST /api/copilot/corpus`, `GET /api/briefs`; `IntelligentView` records the engine's reading on the grammar path too. The model's `set_research` example in the system prompt gains the brief's fields.
+
+## Tests
+
+| Suite | What it checks | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| `packages/engine/src/brief.test.ts` | every brief sentence as one action, merged, lists added to, nothing twice, already-so, read back, the change tree's fields, the model's brief through the gate; the planner's objective from the business question and the brief kept by `set_research` | 2 tests |
+| `packages/engine/src/languageCorpus.test.ts` | every repository corpus replays with nothing worse and nothing changed; a corpus from a history (dedupe, counts, the last reading, the first spelling, a revised prompt, sources left out, the grammar's and the model's readings), every verdict, the backlog's order, `describeReplay`, `recordCorpus`, `readingOf` | 2 tests (engine 1772 pass) |
+| `packages/analytics/src/phase8.test.ts` | the KPI snapshot of every measure and what cannot be measured, in the run and the brief; the comparison on a planted second wave (satisfaction up and significant, a lower-is-better KPI worse, a flat KPI, an unknown one; the gender finding weaker, the region finding stronger/new, H2 supported; the summary), the stable key, a run against itself; the brief text, the gate, the slide, the deck order and the brief's client and question on it, the PowerPoint's slide text, the report's section present and absent, the proposal's brief | 2 tests (analytics suite green) |
+| `apps/studio/lib/analyticsRunStore.test.ts` | the three-step insert fallback (Phase 8 columns, Phase 4 columns, bare) and the run carrying what was computed; `pickPrevious` by dataset kind, the stored KPIs and comparison read back | 5 tests |
+| `apps/studio/lib/copilot/copilot.test.ts` | the outline's brief line (and none without a brief); the prompt's size cap raised to 14 800 for the brief's example | extended |
